# ~/.claude — portable configuration only.
#
# This directory is ~100 MB, almost all of it machine-local state: transcripts
# and auto-memory under projects/, file-history/, plugins/, caches, daemon and
# session bookkeeping. None of that should travel between machines, and some of
# it must never leave this one.
#
# So the rule is inverted: ignore everything, then re-include the ~550 KB that is
# genuinely configuration.

*

!.gitignore
!settings.json
!CLAUDE.md

# wss-doctor.sh, the one root script left. `!*.sh` re-includes it; the other
# sixteen moved to `wss/scripts/` on 2026-08-15's tier 2 (already covered by
# the `!wss/` + `!wss/**` pair below) and the hook scripts moved to `hooks/`
# on 2026-08-01 for the plugin layout — `!*.sh` cannot reach either
# subdirectory, which is why `!hooks/` and `!wss/` each need their own pair.
!*.sh

# The plugin layout. `hooks/` holds the hook scripts and the `hooks.json`
# that declares them; `.claude-plugin/` holds the manifest that makes this
# directory installable.
#
# BOTH directory lines are load-bearing and neither is implied by `!*.sh` or by
# the other. Git does not descend into an excluded directory, so a negation on a
# path INSIDE one is never consulted — the same trap the `.github/` and `tests/`
# block above documents. Without `!hooks/`, moving the hooks there would have
# silently untracked both of them and every `--flag` on a fresh clone with it.
!hooks/
!hooks/**
!.claude-plugin/
!.claude-plugin/**

# User-level skills and agents — available in every project.
!skills/
!skills/**
!agents/
!agents/**

# Slash-command wrappers for the flags whose skill carries a different name —
# each file's name equals the flag its body fires, and wss-doctor.sh asserts that.
!commands/
!commands/**

# This repo is two things at once: a live config directory and a project with
# its own documentation, gitignore-only. The inverted rule above serves the
# first and would block the second, so re-include README.md explicitly rather
# than loosening `*`, which would start pulling in machine state again. The
# docs site itself lives under `wss/` as of 2026-08-15 (moved out of a
# top-level `docs/`) and needs no re-inclusion pair of its own — the `!wss/`
# block below already covers it wholesale.
!README.md

# The `/wss` tree: the project's own records, logs, generated artifacts and
# local flags, gathered out of the root, `docs/` and `.claude/` on 2026-08-15.
# BOTH lines are load-bearing for the same reason the `!hooks/` block above
# spells out — `!*.sh` and a bare `!wss/` cannot reach into a subdirectory, and
# a missing pair does not error, it silently untracks. Add nothing here that is
# machine-local: this tree travels between machines.
!wss/
!wss/**

# ...except `wss/flags/`, which is per-machine state by definition — the alert
# switch and its stamp were untracked at the root and must stay untracked here.
# The `!wss/**` pair above would otherwise re-include them, which is the exact
# accident that pair is powerful enough to cause.
wss/flags/

# Without a LICENSE a repo is all rights reserved, which would make the skills
# unusable by anyone who finds them.
!LICENSE

# CI, and the tests it runs. Verify with `git status --porcelain` after adding
# any new KIND of path here, not just a new file. `!*.sh` above cannot save a
# script inside an excluded directory: git does not descend into one, so the
# negation is never consulted.
!.github/
!.github/**

# `$PWD/.claude/skills` is where a project's own skills live, and the workflow
# supports that everywhere — a project ships its own skill and the flag hook
# resolves it there first.
#
# THIS REPO NOW KEEPS TWO THERE, and the placement is the point rather than an
# accident. `skills/` here is the SUITE's, and every file in it loads in every
# project on this machine; a skill that only makes sense against this repository
# — one that names `audits/`, `wss-publish.sh`, this tree's own method files —
# would be dead weight in all of them and confusing in most. Under
# `.claude/skills/` it is reachable only from a session standing here.
# `wss-publish.sh` deletes the directory from every assembly, so none of it
# reaches an adopter.
#
# Narrow on purpose. `.claude/` will accumulate machine-local state — a
# settings.local.json, session bookkeeping — so re-include files by name rather
# than the directory. The first line only lets git DESCEND; without it none of
# the rest is ever consulted.
!.claude/
!.claude/WSS.TOOLING.md
# The catalog's generated twin: `.claude/WSS.TOOLING.md` holds what a tool is
# for, this holds every measured fact about it. Tracked, unlike the derived
# files named further down, because `wss-tools-inventory.sh --check` regenerates
# to a temp file and diffs against this one — with nothing committed there is
# nothing to diff and the staleness guard is vacuous rather than absent. Same
# reason `docs/WSS.DECISIONS-INDEX.md` is tracked.
!.claude/WSS.TOOLS.json

# This repo running its own workflow on itself. Every path below is a record
# file this configuration's skills expect, or the manifest that maps them.
# Whitelisting is not adoption — these lines only permit the files;
# `.claude/WSS.WORKFLOW.json` is what declares which of them are records.
#
# Deliberately NOT here: `.claude/WSS.SWEEPS.json` and `WSS.BUG-REPORTS.md`. Both are
# derived or machine-local, and both are safer absent — a missing checkpoint
# costs one full sweep and can never cost correctness.
#
# WSS.ROADMAP.md and CHANGELOG.md were forward-looking permits until 2026-08-01, when
# the manifest began declaring `WSS.record.roadmap` and `WSS.record.changelog` and both
# files were created. The permits were already right, which is the argument for
# writing one before the file exists: `git add` declines a new KIND of file
# silently, so the cost of an unused permit is nothing and the cost of a missing
# one is a record nobody notices is untracked.
!WSS.TODO.md
!WSS.ROADMAP.md
!WSS.RELEASES.md
!CHANGELOG.md
!WSS.CHANGELOG.md
# Five of the root scripts used to need their own re-include line here, each
# with its own comment — `!*.sh` cannot reach a subdirectory any more than it
# could reach `hooks/`, so each was named individually. THEY NEED NO
# RE-INCLUSION OF THEIR OWN ANY MORE: wss-publish.sh, wss-reset-records.sh,
# wss-export-records.sh, wss-retire-workflow.sh and wss-tree-survey.sh all
# moved to `wss/scripts/` in 2026-08-15's tier 2, which the `!wss/` +
# `!wss/**` pair above already reaches — the same shape the audits reports
# below document for the same reason.
# Agent audit reports. Tracked so they are BACKED UP — they are the most
# expensive artifact this repo produces and they existed on one machine only
# until 2026-08-02, one disk failure from gone.
#
# THEY NEED NO RE-INCLUSION OF THEIR OWN ANY MORE. They live at
# `wss/logs/audits/`, which the `!wss/` + `!wss/**` pair above already reaches;
# the `!audits/` pair that used to sit here named a root directory that no
# longer exists, so it re-included nothing.
#
# They do NOT travel to the published repo: `wss-publish.sh` deletes them from
# the assembly. **Its whitelist is NOT the backstop for that any more** — Gate 2
# admits `wss/` wholesale, so the reports are admitted by it now, and the
# backstop is a dedicated Gate 2 line naming `wss/logs/audits/`. Keeping them
# out of the public tree is that script's job, not this file's — being untracked
# was never what protected the publication surface.

!.claude/WSS.WORKFLOW.json
!.claude/WSS.HANDOFF.md
!.claude/WSS.HAZARDS.md
!.claude/agents/
!.claude/agents/**
!.claude/skills/
!.claude/skills/**

# Never, under any circumstances. Last word wins, so everything below survives
# any re-inclusion added above it later — which is the whole reason this block
# is at the bottom. Add new re-inclusions ABOVE it, never below.
.credentials.json

# The block above protects one filename. The re-inclusions higher up admit whole
# directory trees WHOLESALE — skills/**, .claude/agents/**, wss/**, wss/workflow/**,
# tests/** and .github/** among them — so before these lines existed a
# new sensitive KIND under any of them was committable and nothing said so.
# `git add` is silent when it declines a path and equally silent when it accepts
# one, so the only signal was noticing.
#
# By shape rather than by name, because the next one will not be called
# .credentials.json. Every pattern here is unanchored, so it applies at any depth
# inside those trees. Verified against the tracked set when added: none of these
# matches anything this repo legitimately keeps, and the "Credentials never
# travel" step in CI asserts a representative sample stays ignored, so a
# re-inclusion added below this block by mistake fails the build.
.env
.env.*
*.pem
*.key
*.p12
*.pfx
*.jks
*.keystore
*.token
id_rsa
id_dsa
id_ecdsa
id_ed25519
.netrc
.npmrc
.pypirc
*credentials*.json
*secrets*.json
